## Related Issues

Follow-up to #24998, which documented this difference between
`WorkflowAgent` and `ToolLoopAgent`.

commit.message:
fix(workflow): log provider warnings in WorkflowAgent (#25015)

## Background

`ToolLoopAgent` logs provider warnings, for example an unsupported
setting, through the AI SDK warning logger. `WorkflowAgent` logged
nothing. The warnings were only available as `warnings` on each step, so
a setting that the provider ignored went unnoticed.

## Summary

- The durable generate and stream steps call `logWarnings`, which
`ai/internal` now exports. The `AI_SDK_LOG_WARNINGS` global controls the
output as usual.
- The logging happens inside the durable step. A workflow replay returns
the recorded step result and does not log again.
- The sentence is removed from "Differences from ToolLoopAgent".
- New test file `workflow-agent-warnings.test.ts`, side by side with
`ToolLoopAgent`.

## End-to-End Verification

Both runs used a Vercel Sandbox (Linux, Node 24.22, pnpm 12.14) with a
fresh clone of `vercel/ai` at `71bef690f9` in `/vercel/sandbox/base`,
after `pnpm install` and `pnpm build`. The scripts live in
`/vercel/sandbox/e2e`, outside the checkout.

- Before: the unmodified tree.
- After: this PR's diff applied with `git apply`, then `pnpm build` in
`packages/ai` and `packages/workflow`. The scripts were not changed
between the runs.

No real model API was called, because the sandbox had no provider
credentials. Part A runs the real `@ai-sdk/openai` provider over HTTP
against a local mock of the Chat Completions API. Part B runs the agent
inside the real Workflow runtime with a mock model.

### Part A: built packages, real `@ai-sdk/openai` provider over HTTP

A two-step run with `topK: 5`, which the OpenAI chat provider reports as
unsupported. The script prints the step warnings and what the warning
logger printed, and repeats the `WorkflowAgent` runs with
`AI_SDK_LOG_WARNINGS = false`.

