fix(workflow): warn when WorkflowAgent.generate() stops at the default step limit (#25016)

## Background

`WorkflowAgent.generate()` stops after 20 steps when no `stopWhen` is
set, like `ToolLoopAgent`. `ToolLoopAgent` logs a warning when that
default stops the loop, so the caller learns that the run was cut short.
`WorkflowAgent` stopped without a word.

The warning was left out of the first round because a stop condition
runs in workflow context, where a replay would log it again.

## Summary

- The default stop condition of `generate()` only records that it
stopped the loop. After the loop, a `'use step'` function logs the
warning, so a replay does not repeat it.
- The warning text comes from `logDefaultStopConditionWarning`,
extracted from core's default stop condition and exported from
`ai/internal`, so both agents print the same message.
- No warning when `stopWhen` is set, when `prepareCall` returns another
stop condition, or when the model finishes on its own at step 20. A
`prepareCall` that returns the default condition it received keeps the
warning, as in `ToolLoopAgent`.
- `stream()` still has no default limit.
- Docs: the loop control page and the default step limit table.
- New test file `workflow-agent-default-step-limit.test.ts`, side by
side with `ToolLoopAgent`, and an integration test in the real Workflow
runtime.

One difference in timing: the warning is logged after the loop ends, so
it appears after the step callbacks.

